# TODO - Complete production driver implementation — highest priority

## Owner directive

**FIRST IMPLEMENTATION, THEN CORRECTION.** Implement the complete required
production driver, 100%, before starting the zero-failure lint milestone.
This is the highest-priority umbrella TODO and takes precedence over
lint-only cleanup, speculative hardening and conflicting older hold language.

The owner wants the first notebook run to exercise the entire implementation,
including cross-component complexity. Do not make a partial subsystem perfect
while leaving required paths absent. Failed launch, crash or runtime failure
in an owner-authorized test is evidence for the next fix, not a prerequisite
that must be eliminated through indefinite source-only polishing. Implement
the full intended behavior, then validate to zero failures, pass CI and iterate
on actual notebook logs. Never equate this tolerance of test failures with
permission to fabricate readiness or leave known implementations missing.

The integration agent prioritizes runtime implementation and wiring; other
coordinating agents resolve Clang-Tidy and validator findings without weakening
checks or imposing a serial lint-only hold on the missing source work.

## Required implementation

- [ ] Native PCI ownership/power, mapped registers and complete lifecycle.
- [ ] EEPROM/OTP acquisition, board data and applied RF/PHY calibration.
- [ ] Revision-correct reset, PLL/channel configuration and regulatory power.
- [ ] Actual DMA rings, packet buffers, interrupts, completion and recovery.
- [ ] Native Tahoe Wi-Fi controller/interface and OS packet/event contracts.
- [ ] Real scan, authentication, association, WPA2/CCMP/key lifecycle and traffic.
- [ ] QCA9565 Bluetooth USB HCI/firmware/BLE and Wi-Fi coexistence.
- [ ] Native AWDL/peer-to-peer Wi-Fi plus BLE integration required for AirDrop.
- [ ] Suspend/resume, disconnect/reconnect, partial failure and teardown.
- [ ] All required paths are connected to real callers and included in the
      normal production target, without experimental opt-ins, empty methods,
      passive substitutes or permanently disabled required functionality.

## Acceptance and subsequent order

1. Close this TODO only when every required source workflow above is fully
   implemented and integrated, with no known source-resolvable missing path.
   Focused behavior tests support implementation; they do not replace it or
   prove physical Wi-Fi function.
2. Then complete validator-findings: zero lint/check failures and zero skips,
   preserving all rules and source coverage. Keep CI as the mandatory gate
   before every kernel build of the exact reviewed commit.
3. Then continue edge-case hardening indefinitely and finish the remaining
   TODOs alongside the owner's authorized notebook tests. The owner supplies
   real logs in this conversation; agents diagnose and fix actual failures,
   repeat CI/build/testing and keep the owner-controlled acceptance TODO open
   until the owner explicitly requests its closure.

Hardening must not become an indefinite prerequisite for notebook testing.
This roadmap does not fabricate runtime success or authorize an unspecified
build tag, deployment or hardware action.

## Current evidence and missing source

The native entrypoint now owns PCI, maps registers, quiesces MAC engines,
runs RTC bootstrap and discovers EEPROM/OTP board data. PCI and DMA source
are compiled normally. These implementations are progress, not completion:
native coherent DMA allocation, queue programming and interrupt/completion
ownership are now implemented, alongside source executors for PLL, channel
synthesis, RF-bus grants and RX-only AGC offset calibration. The passive scan
scheduler is implemented in WifiEngine. Remaining board/calibration/regulatory
orchestration must activate those real paths; native AirPort registration,
connected scan/association/packet flow, Bluetooth USB/BLE and AirDrop/AWDL
remain open. The manual macOS debug collector is available for the final
owner-controlled log cycle.

## Integrated native startup progress — 2026-11-10

Commit `90f146f` supplies the native IO80211 work-queue factory/getter and
replaces the controller's always-null logger/fault reporter callbacks with
real CoreCapture factories and owned lifecycle resources. This source is in
the normal production target, called before native superclass start, and
unwound after its stop. Required radio/InfraProtocol/packet/Bluetooth/AWDL
acceptance above is unchanged and remains unfinished.

The same commit implements startup diagnostic selection in the PCI/native
controller (explicit `simpleathdbg=0/1`, otherwise exposed OpenCore DBG/NPT,
normal logging on absent or invalid metadata), and preserves matching Release
dSYM artifacts behind the existing mandatory CI build gate. Focused host
policy tests, strict Darwin SDK syntax for changed native units, scoped Tidy
for the capture/policy code, and exact-KDK native import inspection passed.
There is no new whole-tree zero-failure claim, kext build, runtime verification,
notebook test or authorization change. Keep this P0 umbrella open.
